# .gitignore — AMI LwM2M Node
#
# Rule of thumb: this file lists CATEGORIES, never individual filenames. If you
# find yourself adding one entry per file, the layout is wrong — put the output
# in a directory that is already ignored instead.
#
# History: this file once held 183 patterns, ~120 of them the names of one-off
# scratch files (prj_bisect3.conf, tools/recover_and_test3.py, com11_*.txt) and
# ~50 the shapes of capture filenames, one per bench tool. Both classes are gone:
# scratch files were deleted (git remembers them), and every tool now writes to
# captures/ via tools/lab_paths.py.

# ---- Build output (regenerable) ----
build/
build_*/
!build_archive/

# ---- Measurement data (regenerable by re-running the bench) ----
# One home for every capture: PPK2, FNB-C2, soaks, voltage sweeps, monitor
# history/reports. Tools resolve it through tools/lab_paths.captures_dir(),
# overridable with AMI_CAPTURES_DIR.
captures/
logs/
soak_logs/
results/

# ---- Per-version build artefacts (tools/archive_build.py) ----
# ELFs are ~30 MB each and git is the wrong store, but they MUST stay
# retrievable on disk: RIDs 40/41 report raw mepc/ra and resolving them needs
# the exact ELF of the build that was running (docs/PENDIENTES.md §2.2).
# build_info.txt IS tracked, so we always know which hashes existed.
build_archive/*/zephyr.elf
build_archive/*/zephyr.bin
build_archive/*/.config

# ---- Vendored toolchains and binaries ----
tools/openocd-esp32/
*.exe
*.bin
*.pdf

# ---- Operator-local runtime state (specific to one machine) ----
tools/deployment_ledger.csv
memory-bank/
.claude/
edge/

# ---- Experimental / scratch tools (prefix convention) ----
tools/_*.py

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
